# Additional disk-space cleanup plan — 31 October 2026

The owner asked for further disk-space recovery. These two possible actions
were stopped by automatic approval review and have **not** been performed:

1. Archive approximately 13.85 GiB in 17,134 unchanged, Git-tracked PNG
   screenshots and HTML captures from `docs/evidence` directories dated on or
   before 23 October 2026. The proposed selection excludes audio, patches,
   reports, modified or staged files, links, and files modified on or after
   28 October. Every selected file would be verified in a NAS archive before
   its local copy is removed. Git would show the removed captures as tracked
   deletions, and documentation linking to them would require restoration to
   work locally. The automatic review rejected the action as a broad,
   costly-to-reverse removal of tracked history without specific approval.
2. Archive approximately 8.32 GiB from `build/music`. The running game uses
   separate playable audio assets, but this folder holds original masters,
   workbench data, referenced sources and licence provenance. Restoring it
   from the NAS would be needed for the original music workflows and local
   source/provenance paths. The automatic review rejected removal of the whole
   folder because these potentially project-critical materials are referenced.

Any later approved archive should be re-inventoried because files and Git status
can change. No Git index or history changes were made by these proposals.
